                "Inspiration: Deeply influenced by Hindu philosophy (Upanishads, Bhagavad Gita, Karma, Reincarnation) and Buddhist philosophy; instilled deep pride among educated Indians in their ancient spiritual heritage.",
                "Annie Besant (1847–1933): British Fabian socialist and free-thinker; arrived in India in 1893; became President of the Theosophical Society in 1907 following Olcott's death.",
                "Central Hindu College (1898): Founded by Annie Besant at Banaras to impart modern scientific education alongside traditional Hindu philosophical values.",
                "Central Hindu College became the foundational nucleus around which Pandit Madan Mohan Malaviya established the Banaras Hindu University (BHU) in 1916.",
